SUMMARY:TD Music Tuesdays: DijahSB
DESCRIPTION:TD Music Tuesdays bring a diverse and dynamic line-up of artists to the TD Stage in partnership with TD-supported festivals and programming. June dates feature artists from the LGBTQ+ community\, while July and August highlight performers from TD-supported festivals across Canada and beyond. Come ready to experience an inclusive celebration of music throughout the summer. \nDijahSB is a rapper\, singer\, and internet sensation. A Black non-binary artist\, DijahSB explores themes of hope\, heartbreak\, and personal breakthroughs through their music. Influenced by artists such as Kid Cudi and Lupe Fiasco\, they developed a style rooted in unfiltered self-expression and creative freedom. With a global following spanning Brazil\, Australia\, the US\, and the UK\, DijahSB has built a strong online presence known for candid insights into their life\, opinions on culture and politics\, and the realities of navigating life as an independent artist. \nThis program is in partnership with TD.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/td-music-tuesdays-dijahsb/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://torontounion.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/DJ-NO-logo.png
